# THE ORACLE JUDGE, AS PROTECTED CONFIG: a ModernCI tool pin (backend `tools:` entry
# busbar-oracle-judge, key .ci/oracle-judge.pin). The ModernCI daemon downloads it OUTSIDE any run,
# with its forge credential (the release is private), checks the sha256 for the backend's arch,
# and gives checks only the path, in $BUSBAR_ORACLE_JUDGE_PATH. No check ever holds the token.
# These are busbar-release dev-bin's assets, served by git.getbusbar.dev (busbar-release is private and
# Forgejo-only; `auth: forge` sends ModernCI's forge credential only to that host). aarch64 is the judge for BUSBAR_ORACLE_RELEASE_REF
# a69e783f2f668ff30565587b46abf24e5075d81d (busbar-release #442 one keyed build, #444 key list, #445 worker
# queue, #447 cached checkout re-fetched unless at the pin, #448 premises read event-stream bodies, #449 plugin
# source fetched into a temp dir and renamed into place under a per-dir lock: no worker sees a half fetch),
# built by ModernCI (judge-bin-aarch64, static musl), .sig verified against busbar-release-2026-10-28. x86_64 stays the 151ad095 judge: ModernCI compute is aarch64 only and no x86_64 build of
# d12a08c7 exists. Each sha256 equals BUSBAR_ORACLE_SHA256_LINUX_<arch> in .ci/*.yaml, verified against
# the downloaded assets 2026-10-26. Not a branch file (not .yaml).
url:
